th" "⟨1,1,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-33823" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,2,-2⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-70972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-70972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨0,-1,3⟩$ and $w=⟨1,2,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-5i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨-5,3,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-5,3,1⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-70972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec258eb6c94dc1549530bb4230d77e0f72728e5d4939a4eec01690d066a25c19"} {"question" "q-70972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-70972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-5,3,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨-5,3,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,-1,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,2,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨7,-3,1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-70972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-5,3,1⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-33820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨3,1,5⟩+t⟨3,-9,-5⟩+s⟨-8,9,3⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-33820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨3,-9,-5⟩$ and $w=⟨-8,9,3⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -9 & -5 \\\\ -8 & 9 & 3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =18i+31j-45k \\\\  & =⟨18,31,-45⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨18,31,-45⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-33820" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec258eb6c94dc1549530bb4230d77e0f72728e5d4939a4eec01690d066a25c19"} {"question" "q-33820" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-33820" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-45,13,18⟩"] ["math" "⟨18,31,-45⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,-9,-5⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,1,5⟩"] ["math" "⟨81,31,-54⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-33820" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨18,31,-45⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-70977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $D(6,2,1)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨\\frac{1}{2},1,9⟩+s⟨4,-1,5⟩$ and $r=⟨\\sqrt{3},10,-1⟩+t⟨0,2,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-70977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨4,-1,5⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,2,3⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $D(6,2,1)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $d=⟨6,2,1⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =d+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨6,2,1⟩+s⟨4,-1,5⟩+t⟨0,2,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-70977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec258eb6c94dc1549530bb4230d77e0f72728e5d4939a4eec01690d066a25c19"} {"question" "q-70977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Co