/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $B(-7,12,-3)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨-7,2,4⟩+s⟨-5,3,1⟩$ and $r=⟨-22,17,13⟩+t⟨1,5,6⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-5,3,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,5,6⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(-7,12,-3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨-7,12,-3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-7,12,-3⟩+s⟨-5,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,6⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128536" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec258eb6c94dc1549530bb4230d77e0f72728e5d4939a4eec01690d066a25c19"} {"question" "q-128536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=⟨-3,12,-7⟩+s⟨1,3,-5⟩+t⟨1,6,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨-7,-3,12⟩+s⟨-3,4,2⟩+t⟨1,5,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨-7,-3,12⟩+s⟨3,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨-7,12,-3⟩+s⟨-3,5,1⟩+t⟨1,6,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨-7,12,-3⟩+s⟨-5,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,6⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128536" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨-7,12,-3⟩+s⟨-5,3,1⟩+t⟨1,5,6⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $P(7,-3,4)$ and $Q(5,1,-1),$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨5,1,-1⟩-⟨7,-3,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,4,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $p=⟨7,-3,4⟩$ of the point $P,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\ r & =⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-2,4,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec258eb6c94dc1549530bb4230d77e0f72728e5d4939a4eec01690d066a25c19"} {"question" "q-128761" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128761" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨-3,\\sqrt{5},2⟩+t⟨-4,2,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨2,\\sqrt{5},-3⟩+t⟨4,-2,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-2,4,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-4,2,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-5,4,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128761" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨7,-3,4⟩+s⟨\\sqrt{5},-3,2⟩+t⟨-2,4,-5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-32988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(3,1,5),\\,B(6,-8,0)$, and $C(-2,1,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-32988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨6,-8,0⟩-⟨3,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-9,-5⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨-2,1,3⟩-⟨3,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,0,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $a=⟨3,1,5⟩$ of the point $A,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s\\overset{\\to }{AB}+t\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\ r & =⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨3,-9,-5⟩+t⟨-5,0,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-32988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec258eb6c94dc1549530bb4230d77e0f72728e5d4939a4eec01690d066a25c19"} {"question" "q-32988" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-32988" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨3,-9,-5⟩+t⟨-2,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨3,-9,-5⟩+t⟨-5,0,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨6,-8,0⟩+t⟨-2,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨6,-8,0⟩+t⟨-5,0,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["text" "The plane is undefined"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-32988" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨3,1,5⟩+s⟨3,-9,-5⟩+t⟨-5,0,-2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-33160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $C(1,4,-14)$ and is parallel to the two distinct lines $r=⟨-1,5,7⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩$ and $r=⟨0,3,-19⟩+t⟨-2,-2,-2⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-33160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-2,-2,-2⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,1,1⟩,$ respectively.\nBut ${v}_{2}=-2{v}_{1}.$ So, our lines are parallel. \n\nDespite this fact, two distinct parallel lines still determine a plane. Now: \n\n- from the equation of the first line, we get the point $P$ with the position vector $p=⟨-1,5,7⟩$ that lies on it, and\n\n- from the equation of the second line, we get the point $Q$ with the position vector $q=⟨0,3,-19⟩$ that lies on it.\n\nThe vector $u=q-p$ will be parallel to the required plane. \n\nComputing the coordinates of $u,$  we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨0,3,-19⟩-⟨-1,5,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,-26⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}∦{v}_{1},$ we can find the equation of our plane.\n\nWe know that the point $C(1,4,-14)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $c=⟨1,4,-14⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+tu \\\\ r & =⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,-26⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-33160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec258eb6c94dc1549530bb4230d77e0f72728e5d4939a4eec01690d066a25c19"} {"question" "q-33160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-33160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+s⟨1,4,-14⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨0,3,-19⟩+s⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+t⟨1,2,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,-26⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["text" "The plane is undefined"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-33160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,-26⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $D(3,2,-1),\\,E(3,1,-2),$ and $F(5,1,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =⟨3,1,-2⟩-⟨3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =⟨5,1,2⟩-⟨3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $d=⟨3,2,-1⟩$ of the point $D,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =d+s\\overset{\\to }{DE}+t\\overset{\\to }{DF} \\\\ r & =⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨0,-1,-1⟩+t⟨2,-1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec258eb6c94dc1549530bb4230d77e0f72728e5d4939a4eec01690d066a25c19"} {"question" "q-128745" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128745" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨0,-1,-1⟩+t⟨2,-1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨0,-1,0⟩+t⟨2,-3,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨1,-1,1⟩+t⟨3,-1,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨1,0,-1⟩+t⟨-1,3,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨1,0,-1⟩+t⟨2,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128745" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=⟨3,2,-1⟩+s⟨0,-1,-1⟩+t⟨2,-1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $U(5,3,1)$ and $V(2,-1,-3),$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-4,2,6⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨-4,2,6⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =⟨2,-1,-3⟩-⟨5,3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-4,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=⟨5,3,1⟩$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{UV} \\\\ r & =⟨5,3,1⟩+s⟨-4,2,6⟩+t⟨-3,-4,-4⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b43f3008aab14f6a953bf33be3ba0cd83395466755dcafc72234ad29f35bc13"} {"question" "q-128760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec258eb6c94dc1549530bb4230d77e0f72728e5d4939a4eec01690d066a25c19"} {"question" "q-128760" "field" "sel